  "assumptions": [
    "Small swings: period T = 2π√(L/g) with g = 9.81 m/s², exact in this model and only approximately true of a real pendulum.",
    "The string is light and doesn't stretch, and the bob is treated as a point at the string's end.",
    "No air resistance or friction, so the swing never dies down; the swing angle is fixed at 10°.",
    "Changing the length restarts the swing phase from the current time, so the bob may jump to a new point of its swing.",
    "Large swing angles, where the real period gets a little longer, and damping are not shown."
  ],
  "program": {
    "source": "const g=9.81,A=10*Math.PI/180;\nexport function evaluate({inputs,time}){const L=inputs.length;const T=2*Math.PI*Math.sqrt(L/g);const th=A*Math.cos(2*Math.PI*time/T);return{nodes:{arm:{quaternion:[0,0,Math.sin(th/2),Math.cos(th/2)]},stringN:{position:[0,-L/2,0],scale:[1,L,1]},bobN:{position:[0,-L,0]}},readouts:{period:T,len:L}};}"
  }
